  "question": {
    "text": "Two points $A$ and $B$ move from rest along a straight line with constant acceleration $f$ and $f$ ' respectively. If $A$ takes $m$ sec. more than $B$ and describes ' $n$ ' units more than $B$ in acquiring the same speed then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "8ekUF",
      "text": "\n$\\left(f-f^{\\prime}\\right) m^2=f f^{\\prime} n$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0YCmR",
      "text": "\n$\\left(f+f^{\\prime}\\right) m^2=f f^{\\prime} n$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sBk9S",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2}\\left(f+f^{\\prime}\\right) m=f f^{\\prime} n^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "85hMd",
      "text": "\n$\\left(f^{\\prime}-f\\right) n=\\frac{1}{2} f f^{\\prime} m^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& v^2=2 f(d+n)=2 f^{\\prime} d \\\\\n& v=f^{\\prime}(t)=(m+t) f\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\neliminate $d$ and $m$ we get\n$$\n\\left(f^{\\prime}-f\\right) n=\\frac{1}{2} f f^{\\prime} m^2 \\text {. }\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
